WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.840
Alight our sensor that once cost $75,000 now sells for a few hundred. This is First Principles

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:13.400
Daily, Episode 161. David Hall's Veladine HDL64E. A light detection and ranging unit

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:19.300
spun 64 lasers on a roof rack when five of the six finishers in the 2007 Defense Advanced

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:25.140
Research Projects Agency Urban Challenge used it. The same function, timing laser pulses

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:29.340
to build a three-dimensional point cloud, now fits inside a bumper module.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.740
The change came from replacing a hand-assembled spinning turret with fixed lasers

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.520
and detectors fabricated on silicon wafers.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.580
Each pulse still travels to a surface in returns.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.680
Only the hardware that steers and collects those pulses has been stripped to the minimum the physics

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:54.603
demands. Before 2005, most ranging sensors followed the pattern set by industrial units such as

00:00:54.603 --> 00:00:57.963
used one laser, a rotating mirror, and analog electronics,

00:00:58.503 --> 00:01:00.063
and they were built in small batches

00:01:00.063 --> 00:01:01.203
for factory automation.

00:01:01.903 --> 00:01:03.263
Hall started from that template

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.103
when he entered the DARPA Grand Challenge.

00:01:05.623 --> 00:01:08.403
He gave each beam its own detector and timing circuit,

00:01:08.823 --> 00:01:11.043
then mounted the assembly on a precision motor

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:13.203
so the beam swept 360 degrees.

00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:15.923
The motor, the bearings, the slip rings,

00:01:15.923 --> 00:01:18.563
and the manual alignment of every optical path

00:01:18.563 --> 00:01:20.983
added parts and labor that had no counterpart

00:01:20.983 --> 00:01:22.823
in the raw physics of light travel.

00:01:22.823 --> 00:01:28.343
Low production numbers meant every unit carried a large share of engineering overhead, so

00:01:28.343 --> 00:01:31.583
the price reflected assembly craft rather than material content.

00:01:32.223 --> 00:01:36.703
Engineers accepted the spinning turret because earlier ranging tools had relied on mechanical

00:01:36.703 --> 00:01:41.643
motion to cover angle, and no one had yet moved the scanning function onto a chip that

00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:43.403
could steer light without moving parts.

00:01:44.043 --> 00:01:48.603
That assumption kept the cost anchored to precision machining and hand calibration even

00:01:48.603 --> 00:01:53.383
as the underlying measurement, nanosecond scale time of flight remained unchanged.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.380
Hall's original unit weighed 12.7 kilograms and required repeated hand calibration.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.800
The physical tasks stayed the same.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:06.840
Launch a short pulse, record the round trip time, and repeat across a field of view.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.340
Engineers later asked what minimum set of components could do that task once the spinning assembly

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:12.900
was gone.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:19.220
1. Vertical cavity surface emitting lasers, VCSEL arrays, and silicon photodiodes could

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:24.720
be grown on wafers using processes already running in consumer electronics fabs. Nature

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:29.820
communications notes that the industry converged on VCSEL arrays because they allow thousands

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:34.480
of emitters to be tested and binned on the same substrate before any mechanical packaging.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:40.220
Analog photonics and others moved the scanning function onto optical phased arrays etched

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:44.020
into silicon photonic chips, eliminating the motor and the mirror.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.740
Each consolidation removed a precision mechanical interface that had previously demanded individual

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:50.300
alignment.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:56.100
The sources give no itemized bill of materials for the raw semi-conductor dies or the optical

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:01.320
coatings, so a precise magic wand number cannot be calculated from the research in hand.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.040
That number is the cost if you paid only for the raw materials.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.820
The floor if the atoms were already arranged.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:11.360
Without the bill, there is nothing honest to put in the denominator.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.800
What the research does locate is the multiplier that remains.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.580
Custom driver electronics, the hermetic package, and the qualification testing required for

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:21.960
automotive safety standards.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:26.640
Those steps still multiply the price of the underlying wafer by a large factor.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:31.360
The price path is the evidence that most of the original expense lived in the mechanical

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.320
architecture rather than in the atoms.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:38.460
pictures starting from the energy per photon needed to exceed sunlight noise and

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:43.080
the timing resolution required for centimeter accuracy. Every added motor or

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.400
manual adjustment sits outside that minimum and removing each one shrinks the

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.880
gap between material cost and selling price. That gap is the first principles

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:57.200
ratio finished price divided by the raw material floor. The new ratio is far

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:02.060
lower than the original designs though still well above one because packaging and

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:06.980
certification overhead remain. I will not divide a selling price by a floor the sources

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:14.857
never itemized. High-volume units such as HESI's ATX reached roughly $200 in 2025, once

00:04:14.857 --> 00:04:19.977
the lasers, receivers, and drivers moved in-house and monthly production passed 100,000

00:04:19.977 --> 00:04:25.577
sensors. The trade-off accepted is a narrower field of view per sensor, offset by using

00:04:25.577 --> 00:04:30.817
several fixed modules around the vehicle. What remains hard is the same range and angular

00:04:30.817 --> 00:04:36.017
resolution in fog or direct sunlight while meeting the zero-defect reliability targets

00:04:36.017 --> 00:04:37.317
of volume car production.

00:04:37.957 --> 00:04:42.897
Even with wafer scale emitters, each module must still survive vibration, temperature

00:04:42.897 --> 00:04:47.097
cycling, and the strict functional safety audits that automotive buyers impose.

00:04:47.717 --> 00:04:52.297
Those requirements add costs that the raw time-of-flight measurement itself does not dictate.

00:04:52.977 --> 00:04:57.377
A mechanical assumption can be retired faster than the people who inherited it expect.

00:04:57.377 --> 00:05:01.057
effect, once the steps that actually make the measurement move on to a wafer.

00:05:01.517 --> 00:05:06.517
The motor was never the ranging, it was how an earlier factory tool covered angle, and

00:05:06.517 --> 00:05:09.177
haul scaled that habit because it was the working template.

00:05:09.797 --> 00:05:11.177
The portable test is simple.

00:05:11.797 --> 00:05:12.977
List what the physics requires.

00:05:13.677 --> 00:05:17.817
List what the last machine added so that a human could aim, seal, or sign off.

00:05:18.357 --> 00:05:21.217
Anything on the second list is a candidate, not a constant.

00:05:21.757 --> 00:05:26.397
The same test shows up whenever a rotating or reciprocating element can be replaced by

00:05:26.397 --> 00:05:32.077
lithographic patterning. A fab already knows how to repeat. Repetition is the whole advantage.

00:05:32.717 --> 00:05:36.957
A pattern printed across a wafer does not ask for a fresh alignment on every unit,

00:05:37.457 --> 00:05:41.377
and it does not reload a full engineering overhead onto a short production run.

00:05:42.097 --> 00:05:47.237
Craft cost lives in the piece that cannot be repeated. Move that piece into a process the line

00:05:47.237 --> 00:05:52.830
already runs, and the craft share stops setting the price. What is left is not a reason

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:58.010
to declare the problem finished. It is the next list. Way for scale discipline has already

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:02.970
cut the laser count by more than an order of magnitude. Qualification and packaging have

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:07.450
not yet been pulled into that same repetition. They still sit outside the measurement,

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:12.650
the way the motor once did, multiplying a way for the physics did not ask to be housed and

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:18.030
signed off one module at a time. The signal to watch is a supplier that stops treating those

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:19.230
gates as separate crafts.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:24.610
Which supplier will first treat the hermetic housing and the safety certification as repeatable

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:28.030
lithographic steps, rather than separate handcrafted gates?

